685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (Throughout her career, Dr. Lapucci has combined scholarship with practical restoration experience. She has taught conservation, artistic techniques, and diagnostics in advanced and postgraduate contexts linked to Florence, and her academic and professional activity has been shaped by a constant dialogue between the studio, the laboratory, and the historical archive. This combination of practical and intellectual expertise has enabled her to make original contributions to the understanding of artistic process, workshop practice, and the complex material lives of paintings. Dr. Lapucci is also widely known for her studies on Caravaggio and for her sustained engagement with the technical problems surrounding his painting method. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 333 0 R
/T (Experts Involved in the Authentication Process)
/E (Experts Involved in the Authentication Process)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 333 0 R
/E (Dr. Roberta Lapucci is an Italian art historian, conservator, and researcher whose work has long focused on the technical, material, and diagnostic study of old master painting, with particular expertise in the art of Michelangelo Merisi da Caravaggio. Over several decades, she has developed a distinctive interdisciplinary approach that brings together art-historical research, conservation practice, scientific analysis, and close visual examination. Her work is especially recognized for its attention to the technical construction of paintings, the role of optics and image transfer, the reading of stratigraphy and pentimenti, and the interpretation of hidden or altered pictorial layers revealed through diagnostic methods.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
