/T (Her current work includes the study of the Caravaggio / Minniti case and the forthcoming publication devoted to the painting identified as Archimedes \(1608-10\), a work from a private collection examined through extensive diagnostic and historical research. In her current lecture and publication project, Dr. Lapucci explores the possibility that the underlying image may preserve an abandoned Caravaggio abbozzo later reworked by Mario Minniti, opening a broader discussion on artistic collaboration, unfinished sketches, and the transformation of one pictorial idea into another.)
/E (Her current work includes the study of the Caravaggio / Minniti case and the forthcoming publication devoted to the painting identified as Archimedes \(1608-10\), a work from a private collection examined through extensive diagnostic and historical research. In her current lecture and publication project, Dr. Lapucci explores the possibility that the underlying image may preserve an abandoned Caravaggio abbozzo later reworked by Mario Minniti, opening a broader discussion on artistic collaboration, unfinished sketches, and the transformation of one pictorial idea into another.)
