/T (Dr. Fabio Scaletti is an Italian scholar, writer, and cultural commentator whose work moves across philosophy, intellectual history, literature, and the study of art. His profile is marked by an interdisciplinary approach that does not isolate works of art from the wider worlds of ideas, language, symbolism, and historical thought, but instead seeks to understand them within broader cultural and philosophical frameworks. This breadth of interest makes his contribution especially valuable in contexts where painting is not considered merely as an object of style or attribution, but as a point of encounter between artistic invention, historical consciousness, and the enduring structures of European culture.)
/E (Dr. Fabio Scaletti is an Italian scholar, writer, and cultural commentator whose work moves across philosophy, intellectual history, literature, and the study of art. His profile is marked by an interdisciplinary approach that does not isolate works of art from the wider worlds of ideas, language, symbolism, and historical thought, but instead seeks to understand them within broader cultural and philosophical frameworks. This breadth of interest makes his contribution especially valuable in contexts where painting is not considered merely as an object of style or attribution, but as a point of encounter between artistic invention, historical consciousness, and the enduring structures of European culture.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1]
>>
