724 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 341 0 R
/T (In 2018 I had the privilege of examining a painting together with restorers from the Hermitage Museum. During our discussion they pointed out a minute pictorial detail which, in their opinion, was characteristic of Caravaggio's hand. Eight years later, while standing before Archimedes, I was struck when a dedicated student of Caravaggio, independently drew my attention to a remarkably similar feature beneath the figure's shoulder. Such observations do not constitute proof, but they are the sort of small, recurring signals that remain in one's memory.)
/E (In 2018 I had the privilege of examining a painting together with restorers from the Hermitage Museum. During our discussion they pointed out a minute pictorial detail which, in their opinion, was characteristic of Caravaggio's hand. Eight years later, while standing before Archimedes, I was struck when a dedicated student of Caravaggio, independently drew my attention to a remarkably similar feature beneath the figure's shoulder. Such observations do not constitute proof, but they are the sort of small, recurring signals that remain in one's memory.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [2]
>>
