/P 342 0 R
/T (I have tested this impression repeatedly. For me it occurs with Caravaggio and with certain other great masters, but rarely with his followers. The difference can be subtle, yet it is tangible-rather like the difference between a living person and a perfect wax figure. This, perhaps, is my own definition of connoisseurship.)
/E (I have tested this impression repeatedly. For me it occurs with Caravaggio and with certain other great masters, but rarely with his followers. The difference can be subtle, yet it is tangible-rather like the difference between a living person and a perfect wax figure. This, perhaps, is my own definition of connoisseurship.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [0]
>>
