/Title (Wanting to test whether this impression was merely subjective, I invited Dr Katarzyna Papiez a medical surgeon with no particular involvement in art history to view the painting from the same position. To my surprise, she immediately perceived something similar. Unfortunately, the painting was soon whisked away, and with it the opportunity to explore this observation further and see whether it resonated with other viewers. Whether these impressions can ever be measured is another matter. What I can say is that the painting possesses undeniable power and considerable potential. Some works invite analysis; others invite experience. Archimedes, in my view, does both.)
/Dest [59 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1977 0 R
/Next 1607 0 R
>>
