/Title (Later I sat below the painting, slightly to the right. From that position the image seemed to acquire another dimension of meaning, much as many of Caravaggio's works reveal new aspects of their narrative when viewed from an oblique angle. I am reminded of the Denial of Saint Peter in New York and the Cardsharps at the Kimbell Art Museum in Fort Worth, to name but two examples where Caravaggio's storytelling appears to unfold differently as the viewer changes position.)
/Dest [59 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
