<<
/Title (Her professional activity focuses on connoisseurship, forensic provenance research, and the evaluation of complex, high-stakes attribution cases. By combining exact art-historical analysis with acute practical market expertise, she provides comprehensive evaluations that satisfy both academic standards and the commercial art world. In the Archimedes case, Dr. Gregori provided a critical, independent art-historical assessment and structural valuation of the canvas. Furthermore, she served as the scientific moderator for the Monaco Symposium, playing a pivotal role in publically presenting the painting and orchestrating its examination within an international framework of leading consensus scholars.)
